  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Plains instead of Island on turn 1 means they cannot hold up Brainstorm, the only 1-mana instant in their hand. Having Island available allows casting Brainstorm at end of an opponent's turn to dig for better cards and set up future draws.",
      "action_taken": "Played Plains as the first land drop",
      "better_line": "Play Island to hold up Brainstorm on turn 1, maximizing the ability to dig through the deck early and find additional lands or key spells.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 10,
      "player": "MiMo Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 7,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Howling Mine is a symmetrical draw effect that benefits all four opponents equally. In a 4-player game, you draw 1 extra card per turn cycle but your opponents collectively draw 3 extra cards. This is especially bad when played early (turn 3) as it accelerates opponents into their threats and answers. Meanwhile, Jotun Grunt is a 4/4 for 2 mana that applies pressure and can manage graveyards. Additionally, Gem3F Stoic already has a Baleful Strix on board that benefits from extra cards, and DSV3 Spike has Jet Medallion to cast cheaper spells drawn off the Mine.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Howling Mine, giving all opponents extra draws",
      "better_line": "Cast Jotun Grunt as a 4/4 body for 2 mana to apply early pressure and control graveyards, rather than giving opponents card advantage with Howling Mine",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 64,
      "player": "MiMo Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 66,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Skirsdag High Priest first instead of Mind Stone. While both could potentially be cast this turn (total 3 mana needed, 4 available), Mind Stone should be the priority to ensure mana ramp toward Drana on turn 4. Skirsdag High Priest is nearly useless without other creatures and morbid, making it a very low-impact play on its own. If for some reason only one spell gets cast, Mind Stone is clearly better.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Skirsdag High Priest",
      "better_line": "Cast Mind Stone first to secure ramp toward turn 4 Drana, then cast Skirsdag High Priest with remaining mana if desired.",
      "type": "blunder",
