    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Gem3F Stoic has Krosan Grip in hand and MiMo Vorthos has Howling Mine on the battlefield, which benefits all opponents equally. Destroying Howling Mine with Krosan Grip (which has split second, so it can't be responded to) would deny card advantage to all three opponents while Stoic already has a strong hand with Damnation, Cryptic Command, Mystical Teachings, and Miscalculation. Instead, they chose to cast Sylvan Library, which is a strong card but could have been played next turn after removing Howling Mine. However, Sylvan Library is excellent and playing it early maximizes its value over time, and Howling Mine does also give Stoic extra draws. The decision is defensible but debatable - Howling Mine helping three opponents vs. one player is generally bad for the table, and Stoic already has a full hand.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Sylvan Library instead of using Krosan Grip on Howling Mine",
      "better_line": "Cast Krosan Grip targeting Howling Mine to deny card advantage to all three opponents, then play Sylvan Library next turn for personal card advantage",
