    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Goblin Cadets is a 2/1 for R with the significant downside that whenever it blocks or becomes blocked, an opponent gains control of it. In a multiplayer game, this creature is almost always a liability - it can't attack profitably into any board with blockers without giving itself away, and it can't block without the same problem. Meanwhile, Soul Snare (W enchantment that can exile an attacking creature) provides defensive value, and Windborn Muse (3W flying 2/3 that taxes attackers) would be castable next turn and provides much better board presence. Crescendo of War (3W) is also available and could be impactful. Playing a creature that will likely be given away to an opponent seems low-value compared to deploying Soul Snare for 1 mana, which provides immediate defensive utility.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Goblin Cadets (R) in postcombat main phase",
      "better_line": "Cast Soul Snare (W) instead, which provides actual defensive value without the risk of giving an opponent a creature. Soul Snare can exile an attacking creature targeting you or your planeswalker, offering real protection.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 135,
      "player": "MiMo Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 158,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Ob Nixilis is at 3 loyalty and using -2 brings it to 1 loyalty, making it very vulnerable. The +2 ability would bring it to 5 loyalty (much safer) while draining 3 life from opponents (1 each from 3 opponents) and gaining 3 life. DSV3 Spike already has a decent board with Skirsdag High Priest and other creatures in hand. With Howling Mine giving extra draws, protecting the planeswalker for repeated value over multiple turns could be more impactful than a single 5/5 demon token that costs 2 life. However, a 5/5 flyer is a significant threat in multiplayer, and it enables Skirsdag High Priest's morbid-related synergies and provides a sacrifice target for Infernal Offering in hand. The decision is defensible but the loyalty risk is real.",
      "action_taken": "Used Ob Nixilis -2 to create a 5/5 Demon token with flying, dropping to 1 loyalty and losing 2 life.",
      "better_line": "Use +2 to drain opponents for 3 total life, gain 3 life, and protect Ob Nixilis at 5 loyalty. This preserves the planeswalker for future activations and incremental advantage, especially with multiple creatures already in hand to deploy.",
      "type": "blunder",
