    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Stoic passed priority during combat without activating Sensei's Divining Top. With no mana being used this turn and the Top available, they could have activated it to look at the top 3 cards and rearrange them, which is essentially free information gathering that costs only 1 mana. This is especially relevant since they have Sylvan Library and will want to optimize their draw step. Additionally, with Wooded Foothills uncracked, they could use Top first to see what's on top, then decide whether to shuffle with the fetchland. Passing up a free Top activation at end of opponent's turn is a missed opportunity.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating any abilities during opponent's combat step.",
      "better_line": "Activate Sensei's Divining Top for {1} to look at the top 3 cards and arrange them optimally, especially given the Sylvan Library synergy and the option to shuffle with Wooded Foothills if the top cards are unfavorable.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 174,
      "player": "Gem3F Stoic",
      "decision_index": 204,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Stoic passed priority at end of turn without using Sensei's Divining Top's activated ability ({1}: Look at the top three cards) or cracking Wooded Foothills. With mana available (Underground Sea, Snow-Covered Island, Creeping Tar Pit all untapped) and no pressing need to hold up all mana, activating Sensei's Divining Top at end of opponent's turn to arrange the top 3 cards is nearly free and provides valuable information for the Sylvan Library draw step. This is a consistent value engine that should be used whenever possible at end of turn.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Sensei's Divining Top or cracking Wooded Foothills.",
      "better_line": "Activate Sensei's Divining Top ({1}) to look at and arrange the top 3 cards, optimizing the upcoming Sylvan Library trigger. Could also crack Wooded Foothills to shuffle away unwanted cards before or after the Top activation.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 179,
