      "decision_index": 213,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Stoic passed priority at end of turn without cracking Wooded Foothills or activating Sensei's Divining Top. Cracking the fetchland at end of turn before their own draw step is generally better because it thins the deck, shuffles away unwanted cards, and sets up Sylvan Library draws. With Sylvan Library triggering at draw step, seeing fresh cards after a shuffle is valuable. Additionally, activating Sensei's Divining Top at end of turn to rearrange the top 3 cards before the Sylvan Library draw step would help maximize card selection.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without using Wooded Foothills or Sensei's Divining Top.",
      "better_line": "Crack Wooded Foothills to fetch a Forest (thinning the deck and shuffling), then activate Sensei's Divining Top to arrange the top 3 cards optimally before the Sylvan Library draw step.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 190,
      "player": "Gem3F Stoic",
      "decision_index": 213,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to activate Sensei's Divining Top before Sylvan Library trigger resolves. Top + Sylvan Library is a classic synergy: arranging the top 3 cards lets you put the best cards on top to draw and keep, while putting weaker cards in positions where you'll put them back (avoiding the 4 life cost). At 19 life, optimizing Sylvan Library draws is important.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Sensei's Divining Top",
      "better_line": "Activate Sensei's Divining Top for {1} to look at and arrange the top 3 cards before Sylvan Library resolves, maximizing the quality of cards drawn and minimizing life payment",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 191,
