    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Kardur, Doomscourge is a very dangerous threat against Gem3F Stoic who is at only 19 life. When Kardur enters, all opponents' creatures must attack each combat and must attack a player other than Kardur's controller. This forces Gem3F Stoic's creatures (if any) to attack into unfavorable situations, and more importantly forces other players' creatures to attack Gem3F Stoic (since they can't attack Gem3P Johnny who controls Kardur). With DSV3 Spike having Ob Nixilis capable of making 5/5 demons, and MiMo Vorthos having Jotun Grunt, Gem3F Stoic at 19 life could take significant damage. Gem3F Stoic has Miscalculation in hand which could counter Kardur unless the opponent pays {2}. Gem3P Johnny has only Foreboding Ruins untapped (and Swamp and Mountain untapped), so after casting Kardur for {2}{B}{R} using Temple of the False God + Mountain + Foreboding Ruins + Mountain/Swamp, they likely have limited mana remaining. Looking at Gem3P Johnny's board: Mountain (tapped), Swamp (untapped), Mountain (untapped), Temple of the False God (tapped), Foreboding Ruins (tapped), Rakdos Signet. They cast Kardur for BBRR using some combination. They may have 1-2 mana available to pay for Miscalculation. However, Cryptic Command is also available and cannot be paid around - it would counter Kardur and draw a card. Gem3F has the mana: Underground Sea + Tropical Island + Snow-Covered Island + Island = UUUB or similar, enough for {1}{U}{U}{U}. Letting Kardur resolve when at 19 life with a forced-attack effect is very dangerous.",
