    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "MiMo Vorthos used Jotun Grunt's upkeep trigger to exile their own Brainstorm (a useful card) from their graveyard and Underground River from Gem3F Stoic's graveyard. They had better options available. Punishing Fire in their own graveyard has a recursive ability that could be useful, but Brainstorm is also a strong card to lose. More importantly, they could have exiled cards entirely from opponents' graveyards rather than losing their own resources. They could have picked two cards from Gem3F Stoic's graveyard (e.g., Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth and Tolaria West - both powerful lands) or from Gem3P Johnny's graveyard (Swamp), or mixed opponent graveyards.",
      "action_taken": "Exiled their own Brainstorm and Gem3F Stoic's Underground River, putting them on the bottom of their respective libraries.",
      "better_line": "Should have exiled two cards from opponents' graveyards instead of their own Brainstorm. For example, exiling Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth (a powerful utility land) and Tolaria West (has transmute utility) from Gem3F Stoic's graveyard, or Punishing Fire from their own graveyard instead of Brainstorm since Brainstorm is generally more useful to potentially redraw.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 208,
      "player": "MiMo Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 244,
    },
