    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "MiMo Vorthos sacrificed Soul Snare to Perilous Research instead of a tapped land or Howling Mine. Soul Snare is a valuable defensive enchantment that can exile attacking creatures, which is important when at 31 life in a multiplayer game with threats like Ob Nixilis creating 5/5 demons and Florian on the board. Howling Mine benefits all opponents equally and is arguably helping the opponents more than MiMo at this point. Sacrificing a tapped land (like Izzet Boilerworks or the tapped Plains/Mountain) would preserve both defensive options, though losing a land is painful. However, sacrificing Howling Mine would remove symmetric card advantage that benefits all four opponents while keeping Soul Snare as protection.",
