    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "MiMo Vorthos has an Island in hand and appears to have not yet played a land this turn (or at least has the option to play it). At 10 life with expensive cards like Death by Dragons (6 mana) and Crescendo of War (4 mana) in hand, missing a land drop is a real cost. Having 9 mana sources next turn instead of 8 could be the difference between deploying a critical spell on time.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without playing the Island from hand",
      "better_line": "Play the Island to have 9 lands available next turn, enabling earlier deployment of expensive spells like Death by Dragons or casting multiple spells in a turn",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 382,
      "player": "MiMo Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 418,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Canyon Slough (enters tapped) instead of Swamp (enters untapped) when they have Sol Ring to cast and want to maximize mana for post-combat plays with Florian's trigger and potential Rakdos discount. The extra untapped mana could matter for casting more spells this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Played Canyon Slough (enters tapped) as land for turn",
      "better_line": "Play Swamp (enters untapped) to maximize available mana this turn, saving Canyon Slough for a later turn or cycling it.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 383,
      "player": "Gem3P Johnny",
      "decision_index": 417,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Played Canyon Slough (enters tapped) as the land drop when holding a basic Swamp that enters untapped. This wastes a mana this turn and also loses the future cycling option on Canyon Slough. With a full hand of castable spells, the untapped mana matters for sequencing plays this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Played Canyon Slough (tapped) from hand as land for turn.",
      "better_line": "Play the basic Swamp from hand (enters untapped) to maximize available mana this turn, and retain Canyon Slough for its cycling ability later when card draw is needed.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 383,
      "player": "Gem3P Johnny",
      "decision_index": 417,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Sol Ring should be cast precombat since it costs only 1 mana and immediately provides 2 colorless mana, giving access to more mana in Main 2 for casting Rakdos, Lord of Riots or other spells. There is zero downside to playing it now versus later.",
      "action_taken": "Passed to combat without casting Sol Ring, planning to cast it in Main 2",
      "better_line": "Cast Sol Ring for 1 mana precombat, then proceed to combat. This provides 2 extra mana in Main 2, potentially enabling casting Rakdos plus additional spells.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 385,
      "player": "Gem3P Johnny",
      "decision_index": 419,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Gem3P Johnny has Fear of Burning Alive (4/4) and other attackers against MiMo Vorthos at 10 life. MiMo's board is all tapped lands and a Howling Mine - no blockers whatsoever. Fear of Burning Alive (4) + Florian (3) + Goblin Cadets (2) = 9 damage, putting MiMo to 1. Even just Fear of Burning Alive + Florian = 7 damage to put MiMo to 3. Instead, Johnny skipped the attack entirely, apparently confused by Propaganda-like effects (though MiMo doesn't appear to control one - the Windborn Muse is in MiMo's graveyard). This was a missed opportunity to eliminate or nearly eliminate a player with no blockers.",
      "action_taken": "Skipped the attack phase entirely, declaring no attackers.",
      "better_line": "Attack MiMo Vorthos with all available creatures (Fear of Burning Alive, Florian, and Goblin Cadets) for 9 damage, putting MiMo to 1 life. With Fear of Burning Alive's ETB having already dealt damage, or any future ping, this would eliminate MiMo. Even attacking with just Fear of Burning Alive and Florian for 7 would be far better than attacking with nothing.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 385,
      "player": "Gem3P Johnny",
      "decision_index": 419,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Chose Mode 2 (destroy all enchantments) which hits nothing meaningful on the board, while Mode 3 (destroy creatures CMC ≤ 3) would have killed Florian, Voldaren Scion (CMC 3), a significant threat from Johnny. At 9 life, removing a 3/3 first striker that could be equipped with Basilisk Collar (deathtouch + lifelink) is important.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Austere Command choosing Mode 1 (destroy all artifacts) and Mode 2 (destroy all enchantments), destroying own Howling Mine and Johnny's artifacts but missing Florian.",
      "better_line": "Cast Austere Command choosing Mode 1 (destroy all artifacts) and Mode 3 (destroy creatures CMC ≤ 3) to destroy artifacts AND kill Florian, Voldaren Scion, eliminating a real threat while at critically low life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 398,
      "player": "MiMo Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 431,
    }
  ],
